body: |-
  ## Why
  Two loose ends from the v6.6.0 release that the user wanted closed before next publish:
  1. `architect.agent` had `nickname: architect` as a placeholder — every other tier-1 agent had a real handle, so the architect rendered as an oddball in the roster.
  2. `cartographer` was referenced in `AGENT_TIERS` as tier-1 and had a full prompt in orchestration.ts (line 744), but **no bundled .agent file** — so it never appeared in `paradigm agent list`, never synced, and was effectively a phantom 68th archetype. Worse: orchestration.ts opened its prompt with "You are ATLAS, the CARTOGRAPHER agent" — but Atlas was already taken by devops.agent in the bundled set (a real nickname collision).

  Plus a marketing/discoverability piece: the new 68-agent roster wasn't visible in the README, which still described "a core team of 8 + 3 specialists" — significantly understating what ships.

  ## What changed
  - `packages/paradigm/templates/agents/architect.agent`: nickname `architect` → `Arky`.
  - `packages/paradigm/src/commands/shift.ts` CORE_AGENT_META: fallback nickname `Apex` → `Arky` (kept consistent with the .agent so resolution lands on the same name either way).
  - `packages/paradigm/templates/agents/cartographer.agent` (NEW): full canonical persona — id cartographer, nickname Topo, tier-1, role "Architecture cartographer", rich multi-paragraph description mirroring the orchestration.ts cartographer prompt (arch.yaml maintainer, drift reporter, Mermaid renderer, advisory-only).
  - `packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/orchestration.ts`: cartographer prompt opens "You are TOPO" (was "You are ATLAS"). devops.agent keeps Atlas — the framework now has a single owner for that name.
  - `README.md`: previous "core team of 8 + 3 specialists" paragraph replaced with a full tier-grouped 68-agent roster (Tier 1 / 2 / 3 with nickname (role) interpunct lists) plus the `paradigm agent sync-global` CTA.

  ## Decision the user made
  Atlas conflict: presented three options (restore Atlas to cartographer + rename devops; keep Atlas on devops + rename cartographer; both rename to fresh names). User picked the middle option — devops keeps Atlas (it was the bundled owner), cartographer becomes Topo. Cleanest user-facing change because devops.agent's identity was already shipped to users at v6.6.0; renaming devops post-publish would have churned more.

  ## Bumps
  - `@a-company/paradigm`: 6.6.0 → 6.6.1
  - `@a-company/paradigm-mcp`: 6.6.0 → 6.6.1 (orchestration.ts changed — MCP tool file)
  - Plugin `plugin.json`: 6.6.0 → 6.6.1
  - `@a-company/university`: unchanged at 6.5.0 (no university changes)
